<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Socialist Revolutionary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1902">1902</a>–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Party of Socialist Revolutionaries, Socialist Revolutionaries</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Socialist Revolutionary Party was a Russian agrarian socialist party founded in 1902 that drew on the populist tradition and the peasantry. It won the most votes in the 1917 Constituent Assembly election. During the Civil War its members led anti-Bolshevik governments, including in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transcaspian-oblast">Transcaspia</a> and the Centrocaspian Dictatorship at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baku">Baku</a> in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/socialist-revolutionary-party.jpg" alt="Socialist Revolutionary Party" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: nc161tcs · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Socialist_Revolutionary_Party_poster_1917_detail.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
